🏁 10. Final One-Line Explanation

If architect asks:

👉 “How does binding work?”

Say:

“We issue a server-signed JWT that binds session, request, and nonce.
The client verifies it and includes it in the signature.
This ensures the payload, request, and identity are cryptographically tied and cannot be altered or replayed.”

🔥 Bonus (If they go deeper)

If they ask:
👉 “Why not just JWT?”

Answer:

“JWT ensures identity, but not payload integrity.
Signature ensures payload integrity.
Combining both gives full binding.”
